ll decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 33%.","The business throws off $3.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.36\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 16\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 136% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3596230789899832},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $18.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-18115296.49},{"text":"Significant goodwill (41% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs 