ety -136%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 28%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $20.16 to $144 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 29.1 vs 23.1 and EV/EBITDA 20.5 vs 13.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 40% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.1% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The 21 covering analysts target $175 on average, 28% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.1%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.73).","It runs a 33% gross margin and converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.36x.","ROE of 21% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.9x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 5pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.0% of revenue on R&D and 0.5% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 1.8x net debt to EBITDA ($618.0M of cash against $8.2B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 16.4x.","The current ratio of 0.90 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Goodwill makes up 41% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -1.4% over 3 years, 1.6% over 5 years and -3.8% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 68%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 11.3% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.3% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.26 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 1.1x annual revenue and deferred revenue up 36%.","Capex runs only 0.7x depreciation (1.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and institutions hold 94%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $18.1M sold).","It returns 3.0% a year to shareholders (1.8% in buybacks and 1.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 3.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 38 consecutive years, raising it 5.1% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 84,000 employees, each generates about $306K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 2.4% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $41K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.0M (13x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $1K per employee."]},"profile":{"score":35.9,"head":"Priced 136% above its $58.13 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside its $20.16\u2013$144 range.","pros":["FCF margin 13.3%","21 analysts' mean target $175 (+28%)","12-1 month momentum +35%","Operating margin expanding 1.3%/yr","Returns 3.0% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 136% above fair value of $58.13","ROIC 8.7% vs WACC 9.1%","P/E 29.1x vs sector 23.1x","EV/EBITDA 20.5x vs sector 13.3x"],"flags":[],"vc":{"base":58.13,"base_src":"dcf","bear":20.16,"bull":143.63,"alt_median":30.3,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.9187,"dispersion":0.2774,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 92% above the other models' median ($30.30)"]},"med":{"pe":23.0957,"ev_ebitda":13.252,"pfcf":22.4428,"pb":2.9148,"roic":0.1003,"gross_margin":0.2856,"fcf_margin":0.0681,"div_yield":0.0147}},"mc_quantiles":[6.0,12.48,20.16,24.87,29.96,34.13,39.55,44.66,48.94,54.28,59.6,65.84,72.55,78.18,87.88,97.77,110.84,124.93,143.63,189.47,278.0],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.75,"discount_rate":0.034,"terminal_growth":0.003,"exit_multiple":0.008,"base_fcf":0.206},"ticker":"JCI","dat